      "stem": "Compound A and Compound B are structural isomers with identical functional groups and therefore exhibit the same types and strengths of intermolecular forces. Compound A is highly symmetric and roughly spherical, while Compound B is asymmetric and elongated. Experimental data shows that Compound A has a higher melting point but a lower boiling point than Compound B. Analyze this observation and select the statement that best explains the divergence between their melting and boiling points.",
